esting the reset signal wasn't correctly triggered. The user input on the PC cannot correlate with a manual hardware reset. The log confirms a key signal was not detected during this period.\n\n\nThe system only polled for a specific USB vendor ID and product ID, ignoring that the device was booting into fastboot mode. The workspace includes `super.img` and other firmware partitions. Examining the flashing scripts, `fastboot flash super super.img` is used, while separate partitions like `boot.img` and `recovery.img` are also present. The recovery image seems to have a patched library, indicating unlocked menus.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Get-ChildItem -Path \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\" -Filter \\\"*super*\\\" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object FullName, Length, LastWriteTime\\nGet-ChildItem -Path \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\Downloads\\\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name, Length, LastWriteTime\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"8000","toolSummary":"\"Search for super.img or firmware archives in user profile and Downloads\""}}]}
