{"step_index":514,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:39:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-04T00:39:23-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-04T00:39:23-06:00\nShowing lines 1-69 of 69\n1: # Reporte Forense de APKs del Ecosistema ZTE Híbrido (`B820C-A15 LE` / `B866V2`)\r\n2: \r\n3: Este documento resume los hallazgos obtenidos al analizar las tablas de cadenas (`string_ids`) de los archivos `classes.dex`, librerías nativas (`.so`) y archivos de código fuente `.java.bak` incluidos dentro de las aplicaciones de sistema de ZTE.\r\n4: \r\n5: ---\r\n6: \r\n7: ## 1. Hallazgo Crítico: Código compartido entre Megacable (`B866V2`) e Izzi (`B820C-A15 LE`)\r\n8: \r\n9: Al inspeccionar los binarios DEX de las aplicaciones del sistema ZTE, se comprobó que ZTE compila **un único árbol de código base unificado** para todos sus operadores de Latinoamérica y Asia, activando o desactivando restricciones en tiempo de ejecución según los valores de `MarketCode` y `OperatorCode` almacenados en la partición `/dev/block/conf`.\r\n10: \r\n11: ### Evidencia en `com.ztestb.LauncherCustomize.apk`\r\n12: En el archivo `classes.dex` de `com.ztestb.LauncherCustomize.apk` se encontraron las siguientes constantes y métodos compilados:\r\n13: - **Izzi Telecom (`B820C-A15 LE`):**\r\n14:   - `MEXICO_IZZI`\r\n15:   - `isMEXICO_IZZI`\r\n16:   - `isRestrictedIzzi`\r\n17:   - `Control izzitv`\r\n18:   - `isBootToLauncher()`\r\n19: - **Megacable Xview+ (`B866V2`):**\r\n20:   - `Mexico_Megacable`\r\n21:   - `MEXICO_MEGACABLE_OTT`\r\n22:   - `com.dotscreen.megacable.view.MainActivity`\r\n23:   - `com.dotscreen.megacable.atv`\r\n24: - **Modelos hermanos:**\r\n25:   - `B826C-A16` (variante híbrida hermana del `B820C-A15 LE`)\r\n26: \r\n27: ### Evidencia en `com.ztestb.basecomp.apk`\r\n28: En `com.ztestb.basecomp.apk` se encontró la cadena de registro exacta que explica por qué el `B820C-A15 LE` de Izzi ignora las memorias USB con scripts de depuración (`udisk log`):\r\n29: - `Mexican IZZI market, not start U disk log for broadcast[zte.intent.action.MEDIA_MOUNTED]`\r\n30: - Tabla SQLite de configuración: `CREATE TABLE cfginfo (section TEXT, name TEXT, value TEXT, reserved TEXT\n<truncated 2174 bytes>\ndioservice.apk` y `com.zte.factorytesttool.apk`)\r\n60: \r\n61: - **`com.droidlogic.dvbaudioservice.apk`** ([`com.droidlogic.dvbaudioservice.apk_analisis_dex.json`](file:///c:/Users/CORSAIR/Desktop/xview/experimento/10_ZTE_B820C_A15_LE_COMPLETO/07_analisis_apks_zte_hibrido/com.droidlogic.dvbaudioservice.apk_analisis_dex.json)): Gestiona la mezcla de audio Dolby/AC3 del demultiplexor de hardware Amlogic DVB (`TS0`).\r\n62: - **`com.zte.factorytesttool.apk`** ([`com.zte.factorytesttool.apk_analisis_dex.json`](file:///c:/Users/CORSAIR/Desktop/xview/experimento/10_ZTE_B820C_A15_LE_COMPLETO/07_analisis_apks_zte_hibrido/com.zte.factorytesttool.apk_analisis_dex.json)): Contiene 49,971 cadenas e incluye las pruebas de fábrica de ZTE para el sintonizador DVB (`DVBTest`), bloqueo de frecuencia RF (`lock frequency`), pruebas de SmartCard/CA y lectura/escritura de MAC/SN en la partición `conf`.\r\n63: \r\n64: ---\r\n65: \r\n66: ## 4. Conclusión Técnica sobre la Partición `conf` (`/dev/block/conf`)\r\n67: \r\n68: 1. Tanto en el **`ZTE ZXV10 B820C-A15 LE`** (Izzi) como en el **`ZTE ZXV10 B866V2`** (Megacable Xview+), la personalización restrictiva (`isRestrictedIzzi`, bloqueo de `U disk log`, ocultamiento de Opciones de Desarrollador y desactivación de `adbd`) depende del `MarketCode` y `OperatorCode` guardados en la partición **`conf`** (`4 MB`).\r\n69: 2. En el repositorio [`tohenk__b860hv5-os10-root`](file:///c:/Users/CORSAIR/Desktop/xview/experimento/10_ZTE_B820C_A15_LE_COMPLETO/02_repositorios_github_y_herramientas/tohenk__b860hv5-os10-root) se incluye el binario limpio [`conf.PARTITION`](file:///c:/Users/CORSAIR/Desktop/xview/experimento/10_ZTE_B820C_A15_LE_COMPLETO/02_repositorios_github_y_herramientas/tohenk__b860hv5-os10-root/data/conf.PARTITION) de 4 MB para la plataforma ZTE `g12a_u212_v1` (Amlogic S905X2), el cual permite restaurar la configuración estándar en modo **Amlogic WorldCup USB** sin modificar el `bootloader.img` (preservando la inicialización `BL2` de memoria RAM DDR3 en el `B820C-A15 LE` o DDR4 en el `B866V2`).\r","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":515,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:39:23Z","input_tokens":2590,"cache_read_tokens":152393,"output_tokens":3306,"thinking":"Initial investigation revealed a discrepancy; this needs re-evaluation. The data suggests a possible relationship between the observed behavior and prior findings. Reconsidering the current approach based on this new correlation.\n\n\nInitial suspicion was a discrepancy, but the data showed a relationship to prior findings, so the approach needs re-evaluation.\n\nThe user's request introduces a new requirement: firmware liberation and control box functionality. This necessitates modifying the program to incorporate the liberated firmware's interface, which was previously examined. The focus shifts to integrating the Xview+ firmware interface (including Google TV Launcher, AppDMC, DLStore, Hdplay, Filemanager, XSairec/Xuper Hydra, MXL Movies, MagisTV, Downloader, and Button Mapper Pro) into the program's feature set to meet the user's objective.\n\n\nThe Megacable interface's presence on the ZTE box points to a configuration issue tied to specific partitions. The `/dev/block/conf` partition, specifically its `MarketCode` and `OperatorCode` values, appears to determine the interface's behavior. When altered by the liberated firmware's configuration, the system no longer acts as Megacable OTT. Further investigation of the liberated firmware's launcher and application packages is needed to identify necessary integration points.\n\n\nFocusing on the identified APKs: The Android TV Launcher (`com.google.android.tvlauncher.apk`), MXL Movies (`tv.mxlmovies.app.apk`), and XSairec TV (`com.xuper.netxxus.apk` along with `xuper_hydra.apk`) require integration. Their functionalities within the liberated firmware need to be mapped to the existing program structure. The Xuper Hydra APK, specifically, has a key role with its active servers.\n\n\nConsidering additional APKs for integration: `com.control.device` (Khiv), `TVLauncher_4_GoogleTV.apk`, `Home_Screen_Launcher_1.1.3.apk`, `AppDMC.apk`, `DLStore.apk`, `Hdplay.apk`, `Filemanager.apk`, `Button_Mapper_Pro_2.54.apk`, `Downloader_2.0.4.apk`, `signMagisTV_APS-MUTO.apk` and `autostart.apk`. This comprehensive list requires mapping their functions and interactions within the program. The Android TV launcher and setting the default home launcher are key steps.\n\n\nThe absence of the `super.img` file necessitates a different approach. Simply flashing individual images will not fully remove the Megacable configuration. The program must incorporate a method to liberate and install the Xview firmware interface to override the existing system partitions. The Xview firmware packages, including the Android TV Launcher, are essential for achieving the user's objective.\n\n\nFocus shifts to removing Megacable's lock packages after establishing the Xview firmware interface. The objective involves setting the Android TV/Google TV Launcher as the default home activity while disabling Megacable's applications. This would likely be part of the final configuration step. It's likely the liberation process starts with these steps.\n\n\n\nThe device's `U-Boot` environment indicates a locked state, preventing direct flashing of firmware via `fastboot`. The critical question is how to modify system partitions, specifically `/dev/block/env`, and install the Xview firmware interface externally given the lock state. Exploring all external channels of communication available is essential, particularly given the `lock=10001000` value in `/dev/block/env`.\n\n\nThe `fastboot reboot` command issued immediately after the user's key press likely preempted the hardware reset sequence, thus failing to enter `InUsbBurn` mode. A delay is needed, allowing the user to physically reset the device concurrently with the PC command. Adding a countdown before the `fastboot reboot` command, tied to audible and visual cues, is likely the most effective solution.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"150","Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\experimento\\\\13_CAPTURA_UART_TTL_SMARTTY\\\\SECUENCIA_ARRANQUE_CONTIGUA_UART.txt\"","StartLine":"1"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"150","Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\experimento\\\\14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY\\\\LECTURA_LIMPIA_FASTBOOT_Y_ARRANQUE.txt\"","StartLine":"1"}}]}
